text:
Quality score: 6.5/10.

The code is compact, readable, and has a useful test suite: `python -m pytest -q` passes with 61 tests. I would not approve it as-is, mainly because ingest/update ordering can corrupt the stored “latest” job state, and reporting commands can silently create empty databases when pointed at the wrong path.

Estimated rewrite/significant-change size: about 90 LOC, mostly in lifecycle ranking/upsert conflict handling, parser validation, report DB opening semantics, and schema/index work.

```json
{
  "score": 6.5,
  "issues": [
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/db.py",
      "lines": "31-41",
      "severity": "high",
      "description": "Unknown Slurm states are treated as terminal, so transient states can block later legitimate lifecycle updates."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/db.py",
      "lines": "70-81",
      "severity": "high",
      "description": "Same-rank records do not compare timestamps, allowing older RUNNING or terminal rows to overwrite newer job data."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/cli.py",
      "lines": "121-180",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Report and top commands call the same create-if-missing DB path as ingest, so a typo silently creates an empty database."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/db.py",
      "lines": "52-58",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Database connection always initializes schema and parent directories, with no read-only/open-existing mode for reporting workflows."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/parser.py",
      "lines": "148-163",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Parser accepts negative CPU/GPU allocations and empty user or partition fields, which can produce nonsensical reports."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/reports.py",
      "lines": "14-16",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Failure classification is hard-coded narrowly and misses common Slurm failure-like states such as NODE_FAIL, BOOT_FAIL, PREEMPTED, and DEADLINE."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/reports.py",
      "lines": "58-68",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Usage reports filter with COALESCE over text timestamps, preventing efficient indexed range scans as the jobs table grows."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/db.py",
      "lines": "13-27",
      "severity": "low",
      "description": "Schema has no indexes for reference-time or report grouping queries, so all reporting paths will trend toward full table scans."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/parser.py",
      "lines": "123-124",
      "severity": "low",
      "description": "Timezone-aware timestamps are preserved as text instead of normalized, so lexicographic comparisons can disagree with chronological order."
    }
  ],
  "lines_to_rewrite": 90,
  "approve": false
}
